    "done_when": "tests/test_a_fenced_worker_can_commit.py passes against a synthetic repository and linked worktree under a synthetic code root, never touching a real checkout: inside a real bwrap fence composed by fence_argv for that worktree, git commit --allow-empty succeeds and the new commit is reachable from the worktree HEAD; inside the same fence, writing the main checkout's index, its refs/heads and a file in its working tree each fails; the test skips with a stated reason only when bwrap is unavailable; the declared negative control is executed and logged; the gate adds no failures over tests/test_launch_plan_fences_the_home.py, tests/test_each_run_owns_its_harness_home.py and tests/test_harness_home_carries_the_operator_config.py against base f01992d3; the change is committed in this worktree; the evidence record carries an anchor",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make a fenced worker able to commit in its own worktree by adding that worktree's git directory and its repository's shared object store to the fence's writable roots in reckon/_backends.py (fence_argv near line 1983, protected_paths near line 1887), while keeping every other part of the sealed checkout read-only. Measured by reckon-ee with fence_argv around a test -w probe on 2026-09-25 for the worktree of watcher-seat-survives-other-hosts: the worktree itself is writable, but /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.git/worktrees/watcher-seat-survives-other-hosts (HEAD, index, logs), /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.git/objects and /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.git/refs/heads are read-only. protected_paths names every checkout with a .git under the code root as a read-only overlay, and the write roots re-open only the worktree, the manifest directory, the declared writable directories and the lock directory. A detached-HEAD commit needs exactly the worktree's own git directory, as git rev-parse --git-dir reports it, and the objects directory under git rev-parse --git-common-dir writable. The object store is content-addressed and append-only, so granting it cannot rewrite another tree's history. refs/heads, the main checkout's index and its working tree stay sealed.",
